abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the Data-Centric Trust Pipeline — a four-layer
  governance framework (Integrity, Fairness, Synthesis, Provenance) for
  trustworthy AI in sensitive domains. Includes empirical validation on the
  Adult Census Income and ProPublica COMPAS datasets, the four-protocol
  validation structure for synthetic data (P1 distributional invariance,
  P2 fairness delta, P3 cryptographic provenance, P4 domain plausibility),
  and a decision-level provenance graph with auditable rationale records.
keywords:
  - trustworthy AI
  - data governance
  - algorithmic fairness
  - synthetic data
  - data provenance
  - accountability
  - data-centric AI
